Frequently Asked Questions

Q: What can I do with Gardarr under this license?

A: You can:
   - Use Gardarr for personal or internal business purposes
   - Modify the source code
   - Create derivative works
   - Contribute to the project
   - Distribute the software
   - Use it for educational purposes
   - Include it in non-commercial open-source projects

Q: What is restricted under this license?

A: You cannot offer Gardarr or substantially similar functionality as a
   commercial hosted service or SaaS product competing directly with
   official Gardarr offerings.

Q: When will Gardarr become fully open source?

A: On February 2, 2029, this version of Gardarr will automatically convert
   to the Apache License 2.0, a permissive open-source license that allows
   unrestricted use, including commercial use.

Q: Can I use Gardarr in my company?

A: Yes! Self-hosting Gardarr for internal company use is explicitly allowed.
   The restriction only applies to offering Gardarr as a competing commercial
   service to third parties.

Q: Can I contribute to Gardarr?

A: Absolutely! We welcome contributions. All contributions are subject to
   this license and will also convert to Apache 2.0 on the Change Date.

Q: Can I fork Gardarr?

A: Yes, you can fork and modify Gardarr. Your fork must also comply with
   this license until the Change Date, at which point it will be under
   Apache 2.0.

